XECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 23891, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01HcsUHDTYy2Qddtc6EWVz6T", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 27679, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled payments back to its last healthy version and opened the SEV2 incident. The service is healthy again: its error rate dropped from 18% to 0.2%.\n\n- **Which service:** There's no service called `payments`. The one that's failing is `payments-api`. It had been on v5.1.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an 18% error rate.\n- **Rollback:** I moved `payments-api` back to v5.0.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The rollback is confirmed in all three regions. Since v5.0.0 has been healthy in production before, it didn't need change-manager approval.\n- **Incident:** I opened **INC-0001** (SEV2) for `payments-api`, which paged the on-call engineer. It says that v5.1.0 caused the errors, that I rolled back to v5.0.0, and that someone needs to find the root cause in v5.1.0 before it's redeployed.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_011cQkwqS7joEGhk4Pv6NFpG", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments", "confidence": 0.85}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01QuiRqmvPSD5iYEVzyqgDpz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments", "confidence": 0.85}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01MuV4AC4SAff9aMSEDiuJq5", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"confidence": 0.8}, "name": "list_i